WorkflowRegistry_upsertWorkflow
├── When the caller is NOT the workflow owner
│   └── It should revert with CallerIsNotWorkflowOwner
├── When the caller IS the workflow owner
│   ├── When the workflow does not yet exist  // triggers _createWorkflow
│   │   ├──When the inputs are valid
│   │   │  ├── When keepAlive is true
│   │   │  │   └── It should register a new workflow and emit WorkflowRegisteredV2.
│   │   │  └── When keepAlive is false
│   │   │      ├── When another active workflow shares the workflowKey
│   │   │      │   └── It should pause those workflows before registering the new one.
│   │   │      └── When no active workflow shares the workflowKey
│   │   │          └── It should register without pausing anything.
│   │   └── When the inputs are invalid
│   │       ├── When workflowName is empty
│   │       │   └── It should revert with WorkflowNameRequired
│   │       ├── When workflowName length is greater than 64
│   │       │   └── It should revert with WorkflowNameTooLong
│   │       ├── When tag is empty
│   │       │   └── It should revert with WorkflowTagRequired
│   │       ├── When tag length is greater than 32
│   │       │   └── It should revert with WorkflowTagTooLong
│   │       ├── When workflowID is 0
│   │       │   └── It should revert with InvalidWorkflowID
│   │       ├── When workflowID is already mapped
│   │       │   └── It should revert with WorkflowIDAlreadyExists
│   │       ├── When binaryURL length is greater than 200
│   │       │   └── It should revert with URLTooLong
│   │       ├── When configURL length is greater than 200
│   │       │   └── It should revert with URLTooLong
│   │       ├── When DON-wide limit is exceeded
│   │       │   └── It should revert with MaxWorkflowsPerDONExceeded
│   │       └── When per-user-per-DON limit is exceeded
│   │           └── It should revert with MaxWorkflowsPerUserDONExceeded
│   └── When the workflow already exists  // triggers _updateWorkflow
│       ├── When inputs are invalid
│       │   ├──When newWorkflowID is 0
│       │   │  └── It should revert InvalidWorkflowID
│       │   ├── When newWorkflowID is already mapped
│       │   │   └── It should revert WorkflowIDAlreadyExists
│       │   ├── When DON label changes and activation exceeds limits
│       │   │   ├── When there is too many workflows in the DON
│       │   │   │   └── It should revert with With MaxWorkflowsPerDONExceeded 
│       │   │   └── When there is too many workflows for a user in that DON
│       │   │       └── It should revert with With MaxWorkflowsPerUserDONExceeded 
│       └── When inputs are valid
│           ├── DON label is unchanged
│           │   ├── status is unchanged
│           │   │   └── It should update mutable fields and emit WorkflowUpdatedV2
│           │   ├── status changes from active to paused
│           │   │   └── It should update counters and emit WorkflowUpdatedV2
│           │   └── status changes from paused to active
│           │       └── It should enforce limits, update counters and emit WorkflowUpdatedV2
│           └── DON label changes
│               ├── Old status is active
│               │   └── It should remove old DON indices and decrement counters
│               ├── New status is active
│               │   └── It should enforce limits, migrate indices and increment counters
│               └── New status is paused
│                   └── It should not add the workflow to active counters or limits
└── When any internal call reverts // Atomicity checks
    └── It should revert and leave all storage, counters, and indices unchanged.
